{
 "_note": "Hand fixes merged over the analyzed masks (tools/plate_prep.py). falls_fireflies: the weather Truman chose is a clear night with fireflies, and the analysis gave them one box over the middle jungle; this second box takes them around the falls and the far cliff, under every analyzed region (never the pool's, the vines' or the sky's pixels). left_hanging_vines replaces the analyzed region of that name: the vines cover the left pillar's whole face like ivy climbing from the floor, so they are pinned at the bottom and rustle (scene.json: 4 px at 0.25 Hz); pinned at the top, their upper part could never move, and a bigger swing would move the stone. sky_hanging_vines: a strand hanging in the open sky at x 0.68 that the analysis missed (the static check found it still), pinned at its top. lift: the four strands hanging free in front of the view (the two long ones, the thin one and the one in the sky) are lifted onto their own layer by tools/vine_layers.py and swing in vines.js (Truman asked for the front vines to move more, 2026-10-27); lift_clean repaints the view behind them in two bands, one edit window each; lift_sky (written by the tool) is the sky behind them. moon: the painted moon and its glitter on the pool come off the plate (cozy/plate/moon.py) and plate.js draws them crossing the sky (scene.json plate_fx.moon; Truman asked for the moon to move, 2026-10-27).",
